-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Lode Runner
  Publisher   Software Projects, 1984
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Lode Runner (1984)(Software Projects)(128K).z80
  MD5         41360f6c33e7a02ca6450881cb385ade

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Based on the Spec256 colours, with a white runner. Also changed
              from them: shaded runner and guards, shaded orange-red bricks,
              cyan ladders with a light and a dark rail, gold as a solid
              bright bar, a shadow under the yellow bars, shaded status bar.
              Optional with it: Backdrop, the Spec256 night picture dimmed
              behind the level. Source: Enhanced colours: Spec256 team
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Lode Runner engine rebuilt on the 128K
              release (AY music), with the whole alt ROM image and the start-
              up checks. 1.1: Enhanced colours, an option on the menu;
              Backdrop, an option with it; the tape's loading screen; R left
              as the original's at every hook; the level editor keeps its
              start positions and guards, which 1.0 lost on leaving the editor

  Note        Keys: menu 1 keyboard, 0 start, any key begins a level; I left,
              P right, Q up, A down, N and M dig; menu 5 redefines. The 128K
              release, AY music. Default: Dean Woodyatt's engine, runner and
              guards as hardware sprites in the game's colours. Enhanced
              (off): a white runner, shaded guards, bricks, ladders and gold
              on the tile layer. Backdrop (off; turning it on turns Enhanced
              on): a dimmed night picture behind the level, title and menus.
              Known issues: pace in JNext against the original, 5 seeds a
              scene, in lockstep: whole runs default +0.00 to +0.15%, Enhanced
              and Backdrop -0.20 to +0.00%, slowest 20 updates +0.20%. In
              Enhanced, bricks being dug or refilling show the game's red
              frames; between lives the scenery stays up while the text fades;
              the level editor keeps the game's colours. Missing: a guard
              carrying gold looks like the others; tape load and save not run;
              level complete and the hall of fame by a test copy only; the
              editor's Test and Move, Kempston, Interface 2 and Cursor
              unchecked; hardware untested.

